1f:["$","h2",null,{"className":"scroll-mt-24","id":"initial-prompt","children":"Initial prompt"}]
29:T422,Rebuild the attached desktop interface as a responsive customer support inbox for a small ecommerce team.

Use the screenshot as the visual reference for:

- Overall density and three-region layout
- Typography scale and row rhythm
- Border, surface, and selected-state treatment
- Compact header and filter control styling

Do not copy brand names, private data, or decorative content from the screenshot.

The working product must include:

- An inbox list with customer, subject, channel, priority, assignee, and time
- Search plus channel, status, and assignee filters
- A selected conversation view with message history and customer context
- A reply composer with send, internal note, and attachment states
- Loading, no-results, no-selection, draft, sending, sent, and error states

Preserve filter and draft state when moving between conversations. At tablet and mobile widths, keep the inbox and conversation usable as separate navigable views. Prioritize fidelity to the screenshot's hierarchy and density while meeting these behavior requirements.20:["$","$L28",null,{"title":"Screenshot-led redesign","text":"$29"}]
21:["$","h2",null,{"className":"scroll-mt-24","id":"what-to-compare","children":"What to compare"}]
22:["$","p",null,{"children":"Review the result against both the screenshot and the product brief:"}]
23:["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Does the first viewport preserve the reference’s hierarchy and density?"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Do type sizes, borders, radii, and selected states feel consistent?"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Is the screenshot treated as a reference rather than shipped as static UI?"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Do search, filters, selection, and reply states actually work?"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Does the mobile layout preserve the task instead of shrinking the desktop canvas?"}],"\n"]}]
